.TH EQNORBITALTEST 1
.SH NAME
eqnorbitaltest \- test a real command-module Danby model end to end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eqnorbitaltest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Eqnorbitaltest
fetches
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)'s
own script text through its real in-process
.B run()
seam \(em a test-only entry point, the same justification
.IR hoc (2)'s
own
.B run(argv):
.RI ( string , int )
has \(em then parses and drives it with an INDEPENDENTLY WRITTEN copy
of the same small grammar, checking against the SAME text the running
model actually executes rather than a copy that could silently drift
from it. Two independent implementations of the same grammar reaching
the same known-correct physics is a stronger check than one
implementation calling itself twice.
.PP
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)'s
own
.B run()
also actually executes its script (via the same
.B cmd()
dispatcher
.B init()
uses) before handing back the text, so a caller of
.B run()
learns whether the script is well-formed, not just what it says \(em
.B eqnorbitaltest
treats a false
.I ok
result as a failure in its own right.
.PP
Checks both components of the
.RB \*(lq derivative
vx\*(rq/\*(lqderivative vy\*(rq
lines (central gravity plus atmospheric drag) and both
.B observable
values, all pulled from the model's own currently-printed script text,
not a copy pasted into this test. Like
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)
itself, this file never loads or names
.IR eqn2hoc (2)
\(em it compiles eqn(7) source via
.IR hoc (2)'s
own
.BR compileeqn() .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/eqnorbitaltest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-aerobraking (1),
.IR eqn2hoc (2),
.IR hoc (2),
.IR danbyeqnall (1)
.SH BUGS
Only pulls out
.BR param / derivative / eq
lines \(em not a full reimplementation of every command
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)'s
own grammar has
.RB ( bodylabels / mass / state / observable
aren't needed for this specific check, though
.B observable
values are cross-checked indirectly since this model's two
observables are themselves bare
.B eq
names).
